    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d568">

                <pb facs="0526" n="452" xml:id="pg452"/>

                <head>Mr. Hunter to Mr.
                        Burlingame</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 143.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1865-06-06"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >June</hi> 6, 1865.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> Your despatch of the 7th of March last, No.
                    100, with its accompanying copies of a correspondence in the case of Mr. Mills,
                    who appears to have rented a house in Tangchan, thereby exceeding the privileges
                    accorded to foreigners by the treaty, has been received, and your proceedings in
                    the matter are approved.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>W. HUNTER, <hi rendition="#italic">Acting
                    Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Anson Burlingame,</hi> Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c.,&amp;c.,&amp;c.,</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
